@DavidZagury Thanks for the heads up - I wasn't aware of the merge restriction. Here's the one-liner addition that goes after the telemetry line, in case anyone is interested:
```
{%- if include_system_otel == "y" %}{% do features.append(("otel", "disabled", false, "enabled")) %}{% endif %}
```

@qiluo-msft this is a change in SONiC Arch which was not discussed at least that i am aware of.
every feature we added in the past (and including in the HFT desig) was upside to controlled by the feature command and if the feature is added to SONiC it was expected to be added as part of the implementation even with disabled by default.

We had also discussion on quality guarantee that this is the way to add features to SONiC as initial stage while it is being disabled. this cannot be just a user responsibility.

@lguohan could you please also help to understand the motivation of this arch change ? how can we see the new guidelines for new HLDs?

I rethink of this issue, previously we made a decision to keep minigraph parser behavior by blocking PR changes specific files https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/blob/55b6a69b7ca5bfd7357361875c4d3d07f780fb30/.github/workflows/protect-file.yml#L27.

However, in general, any new feature requires an entry inside FEATURE table, so people still want to add it into 'files/build_templates/init_cfg.json.j2'.This kind of new entry is okay as long as they are by default disabled. The behavior is still backward-compatible.

@DavidZagury @Bojun-Feng Do you have a PR? I think we can go ahead with proposed change.
